WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.564
A robot brain

00:00:01.376 --> 00:00:02.590
trained only in

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.298
simulation

00:00:03.822 --> 00:00:05.024
SenseTime released

00:00:04.836 --> 00:00:07.442
SenseNova RoboRSI 27B

00:00:07.631 --> 00:00:08.751
a robot agent

00:00:08.563 --> 00:00:09.152
model

00:00:09.235 --> 00:00:10.296
with open weights

00:00:10.166 --> 00:00:12.171
under Apache 2.0

00:00:12.694 --> 00:00:13.660
With no real

00:00:13.472 --> 00:00:14.486
robot data in

00:00:14.298 --> 00:00:15.571
embodied post training

00:00:15.784 --> 00:00:16.715
the same weights

00:00:16.527 --> 00:00:17.399
ran on two

00:00:17.211 --> 00:00:18.236
physical arms

00:00:18.307 --> 00:00:19.521
and stacked blocks

00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:20.146
on a Piper

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:20.901
X in nine

00:00:20.713 --> 00:00:21.774
of ten trials

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:23.418
It chooses between

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:24.196
a vision language

00:00:24.044 --> 00:00:25.293
action policy and

00:00:25.128 --> 00:00:26.012
writing code

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.934
rejects bad trajectories

00:00:27.746 --> 00:00:28.890
and replans

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:30.361
SenseTime reports a

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.587
RoboDojo score of

00:00:31.411 --> 00:00:34.453
34.7 against 27.6

00:00:34.265 --> 00:00:35.939
for GPT-6 Astra

00:00:36.462 --> 00:00:37.476
Full story on

00:00:37.287 --> 00:00:38.183
the dashboard
